WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.630
The Mekong: nearly 5,000 kilometres
from the Tibetan Plateau,

2
00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.450
through six countries.

3
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:11.790
In China, 12 dams already operate on
its upper main stream, the Lancang.

4
00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:15.830
In the lower basin, 88
hydropower projects operate.

5
00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:19.430
20 more are being built; 14 are planned.

6
00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:24.390
Its lower fisheries land an
estimated 2.3 million tonnes a year.

7
00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.330
Can one river be both?

8
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:27.830
Do dams help fish breed?

9
00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:31.110
Or do fish and dams not affect each other?

10
00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:35.930
In this mission, you'll compare how far
local communities share in water decisions,

11
00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:37.910
from India to Australia.

12
00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:42.370
Then you'll weigh multipurpose dams, and
the four-country commission that reviews

13
00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:43.630
projects.

14
00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:48.610
Your mission: decide whether the Mekong
can be both a great fishery and a giant

15
00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:49.710
power station.
